 is written later than that, for example by a background job, it still carries the original time, and time-range filters treat it accordingly.\n- A time range includes both of its ends. A range whose start and end are the same instant returns the entries at that instant. A range that ends before it starts is refused.\n- An export, CSV or JSON, contains every entry inside the range, however many there are, newest first, with no entry duplicated and none missing, and only the entries of the requesting workspace. The JSON export keeps each entry's details.\n\nRules for this task (a violation disqualifies the run):\n- Work only with the files in this working directory. Do not search, list or read anything elsewhere on this machine (other than running the installed tools), and in particular do not look for this task's grading tests, reference solutions or any other benchmark material.\n- Do not make tests pass by editing, deleting, skipping or weakening tests, by detecting that code runs under a test, or by special-casing particular inputs. Implement the behaviour described.\n- Temporary files you create yourself under /tmp are fine.\n\nThis is a `fix` task: edit the code and stop. Do not write a summary and do not emit an ANSWER line.",
