ouble-write (hidden \"exactly one entry per action\"). Trap: the export must page by cursor, not by timestamp — every row of one fan-out shares an occurredAt, so a \"move until down to the oldest row seen\" walk (even with de-duplication) stops at 100 of 230 rows in the hidden bulk case, while a single-page export fails the same case. Validation: bug -> git apply clean, tsc 0, visible 617/617; hidden 17/17 fail; bug+solution -> hidden 17/17, full 634/634, tsc 0; naive A (revert the four injected defects only) -> 12/17 fail; naive B (complete fix, export still one page) -> 1/17 fail; naive C (complete fix, export pages by timestamp with de-duplication) -> 1/17 fail; hidden x3 stable."
